    "healthcare": "You are a clinical operations specialist. A 24‑bed medical‑surgical unit with 32 nurses working three shifts (morning, afternoon, night) wants to conduct 40 hand‑hygiene observations per month using the WHO Five Moments framework. Two trained auditors will perform the observations. Describe: \n1. How to allocate the 40 monthly observations proportionally across the three shifts based on nurse staffing; \n2. What specific data each auditor must record for an observation to be considered valid (e.g., shift, time, nurse ID or role, moment type, compliance yes/no, reason for non‑compliance if applicable); and \n3. How to summarize and present the monthly audit results to the unit in a clear, actionable format (including key metrics, trend visuals, and recommendations)."
